Actually — I should check the canon() function to be sure gridRow/gridColumn will match. But since justify-self/align-self already work through it, grid-row/grid-column should too (same class of style props). Let me proceed.

One concern: `el.style.gridTemplateColumns` when PROP_GRID_COLUMNS set it as "repeat(2,1fr)". In happy-dom, reading it returns "repeat(2,1fr)" (what was set). The regex `repeat\(\s*(\d+)` matches. Good. But the SSR emits `grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)` and hydration doesn't re-apply; applyLayout reads `el.style.gridTemplateColumns` from the hydrated element — happy-dom returns the raw "repeat(2,1fr)". Good.

Hmm, but there's a subtlety: in a real browser, `el.style.gridTemplateColumns` might normalize to "repeat(2, 1fr)" (with space) — the regex handles `\s*`. Good.

