The ZStack branch reads `zstackAlignToken(el.style.alignItems)` — which maps flex-start/center/flex-end → start/center/end. But now the ZStack's PROP_ALIGNMENT sets justifyItems/alignItems to start/center/end (alignHCss/alignVCss). So I can read `el.style.justifyItems` (h) and `el.style.alignItems` (v) directly (they're already start/center/end). Let me update the ZStack branch:

```ts
} else if (comp === COMPONENT_ZSTACK) {
  ...
  const h = el.style.justifyItems || "start";
  const v = el.style.alignItems || "start";
  for (const w of Array.from(el.children)) {
    ...
    w.style.justifySelf = fillsAxis(w, true, false) ? "stretch" : h;
    w.style.alignSelf = fillsAxis(w, false, false) ? "stretch" : v;
  }
}
```

And the grid branch: `const token = el.style.alignItems || "start"` → needs h/v. Let me find the grid branch's `setShell` closure which uses `token`. Let me read more.

